WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
TERRY RYAN: Today, we're
talking about GitOps

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:04.560
for GKE, Anthos Ready
Storage, and a new cloud

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.910
region for Korea.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.520
I'm Terry Ryan, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.730
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.490
Application Manager
is a beta add-on

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.720
to Google Kubernetes
Engine that leverages

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.140
GitOps principles to help you
manage release configurations.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.540
This cluster add-on pulls
Kubernetes manifests

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.300
from a Git repository
and then deploys those

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.640
as an application
in the cluster.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.140
Give it a try and let
us know what you think.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.270
The Stackdriver cloud
monitoring dashboards

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.670
API is now generally available.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.070
This API lets you read
configurations, create, update,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.070
and delete dashboards
programmatically.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.950
Now you can easily
duplicate dashboards

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.190
across dev and 2a environments,
or make templates out

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.580
of your favorites.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.503
Anthos Ready Storage
is a new qualification

00:00:50.503 --> 00:00:51.920
for partner storage
solutions that

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.770
have met core requirements
for storage recommendations

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:57.350
and optimal on-prem performance.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.960
These include dynamic
provisioning with Kubernetes

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.410
native storage APIs,
Automatic Storage Management

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.870
across scale up and
scale down scenarios,

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.720
and a simplified
deployment experience.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.330
Check it out to see if these
solutions can work for you.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.650
Our new GCP region in Seoul is
officially open for business.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:17.850
Designed to support
Korean customers,

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.390
the new Seoul region is
comprised of three zones,

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.000
enabling customers and partners
to run high availability

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.867
workloads and store
their data locally.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:27.950
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.950
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.170
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.850
We'll see you in the cloud.

